  "subject": "A flyer-hander outside Mong Kok station has been refused eleven thousand times in six years and is about to give up when an old lady takes the leaflet, reads the whole thing aloud in the street, and gets a crowd to queue for the free tea at a shop that turns out to be closed.",
  "caption": "Cantonese Bulgarian-style women's choir folk-pop, driving asymmetric stomp. A women's choir singing open-throat close harmonies in tight parallel seconds, wooden kaval flute playing a quick ornamented line, tupan frame drum on a driving 7/8 pulse, a drone from a gadulka fiddle. Dry live-in-the-room village hall recording, natural room ambience, minimal reverb. Large female choir, bright chesty open-throat sound, lead voice calling and the choir answering, clearly sung melody on every line. Clear full voice, every word enunciated, steady sung melody on every line. 108 BPM, E minor. Comic, stubborn, cheerful. No electronic drums, no autotune, no rap, no synth bass, no solo pop vocal, no slow ballad.",
  "lyrics": "[Verse]\n旺角站出口 我企咗六年\n一疊傳單 日日派一千\n一萬一千次 人人行開\n冇人伸手 冇人望我\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\n收低張紙 收低張紙\n求吓你啦 收低張紙\n\n[Chorus]\n收低張紙 唔使錢\n免費飲茶 食點心\n收低張紙 收低張紙\n一張紙啫 又唔重\n\n[Verse]\n今朝落雨 我淋到濕晒\n我心諗 今日就收皮\n有個阿婆 慢慢行過嚟\n伸出隻手 攞咗一張\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\n佢戴上老花鏡 大聲讀出嚟\n全條街 停低聽\n\n[Chorus]\n收低張紙 唔使錢\n免費飲茶 食點心\n收低張紙 收低張紙\n阿婆讀得 比我大聲\n\n[Verse]\n排成一條長龍\n三十個人 跟住阿婆\n行到嗰間茶樓 門閂咗\n貼住張紙 話裝修\n\n[Bridge]\n我望住個鐵閘\n佢哋望住我\n阿婆話 唔緊要 我請\n\n[Chorus]\n收低張紙 唔使錢\n今日阿婆 請飲茶\n收低張紙 收低張紙\n我第一次 有人收\n\n[Chorus]\n收低張紙 唔使錢\n今日阿婆 請飲茶\n收低張紙 收低張紙\n我第一次 有人收\n\n[Outro]\n收低張紙 收低張紙\n明日再嚟",
